    {
      "id": 219456,
      "name": "aramis",
      "username": "aramis",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-03T19:50:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"bluedarky\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/48/1975_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bluedarky:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp; the rules do outright state that the players can’t beat her in combat.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It says nothing of the sort. It implies it weakly. It&nbsp;adds a hinder effect upon hitting her for damage…</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PW 67\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n PW 67:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Once she&nbsp;  actually starts fighting, any Attack the heroes land on her&nbsp;  that deals damage Hinders the next hero to attempt to&nbsp;  convince Haka of anything using that Attack’s Min die.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's pretty clear that damage can be done to her, otherwise, it never applies.</p>",
