    {
      "id": 219457,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-03T20:20:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"bluedarky\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/48/1975_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bluedarky:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For the t-Rex you just create a d10 lieutenant, you always roll the environments die pool even if the environment twist you’re planning to use doesn’t use your roll.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't think that's true.&nbsp; I think it's a copy-paste error from the Pterodactyl Thief.&nbsp; Not every hazard involves rolling the environment's dice (see F5 <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#802</span>, for instance).</p>\n<p>It's definitely vague about Haka being invincible, but it does describe talking her down as the only path to success, and her clocking Tempest as the consequence of failure.&nbsp; The whole rest of the adventure assumes the heroes talked her down, though.</p>",
